course: dictionary
lesson: 4823
title: Hurl: strong, sudden action
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word hurl means to throw something very hard and fast. Read the words around it to know which meaning fits. «In storms the waves hit the cliffs with huge force, hurling pebbles.» Huge force and storms tell you the pebbles are flying hard, so hurling means throwing them fast and strong.
explain: Hurl can also mean shouting angry words at someone. People hurl insults when they are cross. If you hurl a rude word at a friend, your voice is loud and your words are sharp. Ask: is someone being thrown, or are angry words being shouted? The clues tell you which one.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The storm will hurl waves at the shore.» Put in throw very hard: «The storm will throw waves very hard at the shore.» It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: Hurl means to throw something very hard and fast.
fact: To hurl insults means to shout angry, unkind words at someone.
fact: Hurling is a fast Irish sport played with sticks called hurleys and a small ball called a sliotar.
fact: In American slang, «hurl» can mean to be sick, but this is casual talk and not the usual meaning.
fact: Phrases with hurl include «hurl abuse», «hurl yourself at» and «hurl insults»; each one shows strong, sudden action.
exercise: «The storm will hurl waves at the cliffs.» What does hurl mean here? | Hide quietly | Paint carefully | *Throw very hard and fast | Sing softly
exercise: «She hurled insults at the referee.» What does hurled insults suggest? | Gave quiet praise | Wrote a short poem | Told a funny joke | *Shouted angry, rude words
exercise: Ella says hurling is a game with sticks. What is hurling? | A kind of swimming race | *A fast Irish sport played with sticks and a small ball | A quiet card game
test: Jayden reads «She hurled herself at the door.» What does hurled herself suggest? | She walked slowly to the door | She painted the door red | *She rushed at the door with force | She fell asleep on the mat
test: Which phrase means to shout angry, rude words at someone? | sleep in | pack a bag | gently tap | *hurl abuse
exam: Copy the word from «In storms the waves hit the cliffs with huge force, hurling pebbles.» that means throwing hard and fast. | *hurling | huge | cliffs | storms
